  "worked_solution": "The center of mass of a collection of point masses ${m}_{1},{m}_{2},\u2026,{m}_{n}$ located at $({x}_{1}{y}_{1}),({x}_{2},{y}_{2}),\u2026,({x}_{n},{y}_{n})$ on the plane is given by \n\n$$\n(\\overset{\u2015}{x},\\overset{\u2015}{y})=(\\frac{{M}_{y}}{m},\\frac{{M}_{x}}{m}),\n$$\n\n \nwhere \n\n- $m={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}$ is the total mass of the system,\n\n- ${M}_{x}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{y}_{i}$ is the total moment of the system about the $x$-axis, and\n\n- ${M}_{y}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{x}_{i}$ is the total moment of the system about the $y$-axis.\n\nSince we require the $x$-coordinate of the center of mass, we need to compute the moment about the $y$-axis.\n\nLet's denote the masses as\n\n$$\n{m}_{1}=6,\\,{m}_{2}=2,\\,{m}_{3}=4.\n$$\n\nThen, the corresponding $x$-coordinates of the masses are\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=-3,\\,{x}_{2}=2,\\,{x}_{3}=4.\n$$\n\nSo, the total mass of the system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i} \\\\  & ={m}_{1}+{m}_{2}+{m}_{3} \\\\  & =6+2+4 \\\\  & =12\\,\\text{kg}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand the moment of the system about the $y$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{y} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{x}_{i} \\\\  & ={m}_{1}{x}_{1}+{m}_{2}{x}_{2}+{m}_{3}{x}_{3} \\\\  & =6\\cdot (-3)+2\\cdot 2+4\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =-18+4+16 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\overset{\u2015}{x}=\\frac{{M}_{y}}{m}=\\frac{2}{12}=\\frac{1}{6}.\n$$",
